pt-gpu-confirm-title = Download the GPU runtime?
pt-gpu-confirm-text =
    GPU parsing needs onnxruntime-gpu and NVIDIA's CUDA libraries. They are installed in Paper Translator's own folder. Nothing else on your system changes.
    • Download: up to about 1.6 GB (much less if CUDA 13 is already installed)
    • Disk space: up to about 3 GB
    • Time: often 5–30 minutes, depending on your connection
    Parsing keeps using the CPU until the download finishes. You can cancel at any time, and remove the runtime later in these settings.
pt-gpu-confirm-button = Download
pt-gpu-remove-title = Remove the GPU runtime?
pt-gpu-remove-text = This deletes onnxruntime-gpu and the CUDA libraries from Paper Translator's folder. Parsing uses the CPU. You can download them again later.

